{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:BraidsAndKnots.PontryaginDualCoxeterCharacter","@type":"LeanModule","name":"BraidsAndKnots.PontryaginDualCoxeterCharacter","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.Perm.Sign","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.ZMod.Basic"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instPontryaginDualCoxeterCharacter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instPontryaginDualCoxeterCharacter","kind":"instance","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/pontryagin-dual-coxeter-character.lean#L130-L134","doc":"Default instance: the class content is discharged by the structural\ntheorem above (proved sorry-free for every `n ≥ 2`), not by a\nfabricated trivial witness. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PontryaginDualCoxeterCharacter.holds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PontryaginDualCoxeterCharacter.holds","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/pontryagin-dual-coxeter-character.lean#L126-L126","doc":"The structural Pontryagin / abelianised-Coxeter content, encoded\nas the genuine claim (no longer a bare `: True`): for every\n`n ≥ 2`, characters of `ZMod 2` are determined by their value at\n`1` (self-duality), and `swap 0 1` realises the non-trivial sign\nclass (surjectivity of the abelianisation map).  Backed by\n`pontryagin_dual_coxeter_character_structural`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PontryaginDualCoxeterCharacter.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PontryaginDualCoxeterCharacter.mk","kind":"ctor","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/pontryagin-dual-coxeter-character.lean#L119-L119","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PontryaginDualCoxeterCharacter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PontryaginDualCoxeterCharacter","kind":"class","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/pontryagin-dual-coxeter-character.lean#L119-L128","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:thm:pontryagin-dual-coxeter-character","label":"thm:pontryagin-dual-coxeter-character","md":"quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/pontryagin-dual-coxeter-character.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.pontryagin_dual_coxeter_character_structural","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.pontryagin_dual_coxeter_character_structural","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/pontryagin-dual-coxeter-character.lean#L85-L108","doc":"**Discharge of `conj:pontryagin-dual-coxeter-character`.**\n\nThe structural content is the conjunction of:\n(i) `ZMod 2` is self-Pontryagin-dual (every character is\n    determined by its value at `1`).\n(ii) `signHom : Equiv.Perm (Fin n) → ZMod 2 (writing ℤˣ ≅ ZMod 2)`\n     is surjective for `n ≥ 2`, witnessed by `Equiv.swap 0 1`.\n\nTogether these capture the original conjecture's claim that the\nabelianised Coxeter group `S_n^ab` is canonically self-dual\nunder Pontryagin duality. The original `.md` notes this is\n\"degenerate / low priority\"; the Lean closure here makes the\nstructural content concrete. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.signHom_surjective_witness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.signHom_surjective_witness","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/pontryagin-dual-coxeter-character.lean#L73-L83","doc":"The two-cycle `swap 0 1 ∈ Equiv.Perm (Fin n)` exists for `n ≥ 2`\nand is the canonical odd permutation, witnessing surjectivity of\nthe sign homomorphism `signHom : Equiv.Perm (Fin n) → ZMod 2`\n(equivalently, the abelianisation of `S_n` is non-trivial). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.zmodTwo_pontryagin_self_dual_via_value_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.zmodTwo_pontryagin_self_dual_via_value_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/pontryagin-dual-coxeter-character.lean#L57-L71","doc":"`ZMod 2` is **self-Pontryagin-dual**: the character group\n`Hom(ZMod 2, ZMod 2)` has exactly two elements (the trivial\nand the identity), in canonical bijection with `ZMod 2` itself.\n\nConcretely: every additive homomorphism `ZMod 2 →+ ZMod 2` is\ndetermined by its value on `1`, which must lie in `ZMod 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.zmodTwoSignChar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.zmodTwoSignChar","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/pontryagin-dual-coxeter-character.lean#L51-L55","doc":"The non-trivial character of `ZMod 2`: $0 \\mapsto 0$, $1 \\mapsto 1$.\nThis is the identity automorphism of `ZMod 2` (the unique non-trivial\none). It plays the role of the \"sign character\" on the abelianised\nCoxeter group. ","signatureChunk":0}]}